# Volt POS — Design System (PC / Back-office)

> Spec for LLM coders building the **desktop / back-office** surface (manager dashboard, menu & staff management, reports). Target: pointer + keyboard, viewport ≥ 1024px. Stack: **Flutter** (desktop/web). Companion doc: `VOLT-POS-MOBILE.md` for phone / tablet / terminal.

The look is **practical, dense, operational** (Square/Toast-class), not consumer-soft: crisp square-leaning corners, hairline borders instead of shadows, one neutral typeface (Inter), one electric-lime accent.

---

## 1. Core rules (read first)

1. **One accent, one job.** `#99FF47` lime means *go / primary / positive / active*. Exactly **one** filled-lime element per view (the primary action). Everything else is ink + neutrals.
2. **Ink on lime, always.** Text/icons on a lime fill are dark ink `#14180E` — **never white** (white on lime fails contrast). For lime *text* on white, use `--accent-strong` `#498F18`.
3. **Borders, not shadows.** Default surfaces are flat: `1px solid --line`. Shadows are reserved for things that truly float (dropdowns `e2`, modals `e3`).
4. **Crisp corners.** Radii top out at 12px. Only toggles are fully round.
5. **Tabular numbers.** All money/quantities use Inter with `fontFeatures: [FontFeature.tabularFigures()]` so columns never jitter.
6. **Density.** Desktop runs tighter than touch: 32–40px control heights, 12–16px gutters.

